  "applicable_autoformal_AGENTS": "# Working on LegalIR autoformalization\n\nStart with README.md, docs/HANDOFF.md and docs/work_catalog.json. The original 24 ordered work items have one maintained home in docs/BACKLOG.json. Update current guides and the handoff in place after receipt-backed changes.\n\nExtend the existing implementation owner and its owning tests. Reusable source, span, graph, review and Lean integration belong here. Numerical kernels and model profiles retain their existing owners in logic/formalization/autoencoder, logic/legal_ir and optimizers/logic_theorem_optimizer; use those contracts instead of copying them here. Public product code must use canonical owners rather than import historical code from artifacts or workspace.\n\nUse the existing source lease for canonical changes and existing native/resource owners for admitted execution. Preserve source-pinned checkpoints, captured sources, failed attempts and original receipts. A relocation is not a new numerical or Lean qualification. Experimental source in the history archive remains an explicit versioned-port task until its compatibility and qualification requirements close.\n\nStore run-specific requests, logs, checkpoints, datasets and generated captures in the existing workspace evidence hierarchy. Maintain one catalog of selected evidence here; do not create another dated implementation or plan tree in artifacts. Read the indexed history only for the specific experiment being investigated.\n\nPreserve unprovided legal source/edition/meaning decisions, explicit assumptions and unresolved dependencies. Engineering fixture passes, authenticated signatures, successful preparation and a native build are separate qualifications.\n",
